 "observations": [
  "body L1-L26: the comparison of the measures, begun on p. 167, set without rules, its column heads repeated; the groups are letter-spaced; braces join the two latitudes of the Sea of al-Baṣrah in the second column and the three latitudes of the Sea of the Romans in the first and the second. Every degree in brackets is the number of miles divided by 75, exactly (8000 miles = 106° 2/3, 1900 = 25° 1/3, 150 = 2°, and so on).",
  "notes_left L12: «L’Examéron» is printed so (Hjelt's title reads Hexaméron, as on p. 165).",
  "notes_left L14: the kappa of «Βαρβαρικὸν» is printed in the curly form (ϰ).",
  "notes_right L13, L18: the 3 of «135» and the last 0 of «800» are printed broken."
 ],
